# Kebu — Task Workflow

For every assigned feature (never invent scope):

## A. Inspect first (no edits)

UI, components, state, APIs, services, DB, migrations, authn/authz, jobs, providers, tests, deploy config.

## B. Report before coding

Exists · missing · broken · disconnected · files to change · DB changes · risks · end-to-end flow · acceptance criteria.

## C. One vertical slice

User action → FE validation → authenticated request → authorization → business logic → DB → response → UI → **refresh verification**.

## D–E. Test and manually verify

Unit + integration + E2E (critical) · typecheck · lint · production build · valid/invalid/logged-out/wrong-user/network/duplicate/refresh/mobile/DB/logs.

## F. Adversarial self-audit

Frontend-only · disconnected API · missing writes · fake success · missing authz · cross-user leaks · races · duplicate requests · broken refresh · weak tests · skipped requirements. Repair before claiming progress.

## G. Completion report

Implemented · files · migrations · data flow · security · tests + commands + results · build · manual · DB · limitations · unfinished requirements.

When asked to audit only: **read-only**; severity-ranked defects; no code changes until assigned repair.
